From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:55:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Declare the unused nanosecond date part specializations
 inline

The member templates of DatePart's operators are declared inline in
their structs, but an explicit specialization does not inherit that,
and two of them are reached by no function the file registers yet:
EpochNanosecondsOperator for timestamp_tz_ns_t and DayParentOperator
for timestamp_ns_t. Inside the file's anonymous namespace,
-Wunused-function reports each as defined but not used. Declaring them
inline, as the templates they specialize are, keeps both definitions
for the day the registration reaches them, where dropping them would
let that day fall back to the generic template without a word.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.
---
 src/duckdb/extension/core_functions/scalar/date/date_part.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/extension/core_functions/scalar/date/date_part.cpp b/src/duckdb/extension/core_functions/scalar/date/date_part.cpp
index ba4656d005..b8fd871d9b 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/extension/core_functions/scalar/date/date_part.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/extension/core_functions/scalar/date/date_part.cpp
@@ -1254,7 +1254,7 @@ int64_t DatePart::YearWeekOperator::Operation(dtime_tz_t input) {
 }
 
 template <>
-int64_t DatePart::EpochNanosecondsOperator::Operation(timestamp_tz_ns_t input) {
+inline int64_t DatePart::EpochNanosecondsOperator::Operation(timestamp_tz_ns_t input) {
 	D_ASSERT(input.IsFinite());
 	return Timestamp::GetEpochNanoSeconds(timestamp_ns_t(input.value));
 }
@@ -1529,7 +1529,7 @@ int64_t DatePart::DayParentOperator::Operation(timestamp_t input) {
 }
 
 template <>
-int64_t DatePart::DayParentOperator::Operation(timestamp_ns_t input) {
+inline int64_t DatePart::DayParentOperator::Operation(timestamp_ns_t input) {
 	return Timestamp::GetDateNS(input).days;
 }
 
